          <div class="section-label">Real-Life Examples</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Real Life — Bank Login:</strong> When you enter your username and password on your bank's website, the bank checks those credentials against its database. If they match, you're authenticated as the account owner.</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Real Life — Passport Control:</strong> At airport immigration, an officer compares your face to your passport photo and validates the document's chip. You are 'authenticated' as the passport holder before entering the country.</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Everyday App — Google Sign-In:</strong> When you log into Gmail, Google verifies your email + password (and sometimes a 2FA code) before giving you access to your inbox.</div>

          <div class="section-label">Step-by-Step Process</div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-text">User claims an identity (e.g., enters username)</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-text">System requests proof (password, fingerprint, etc.)</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-text">User provides the credential</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-text">System verifies it against stored records</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-text">Access granted or denied</div></div>

          <div class="section-label">Strengths &amp; Weaknesses</div>
          <div class="pros-cons">
            <div class="pros">
