          <div class="section-label">Real-Life Examples</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Real Life — Corporate VPN:</strong> When an employee connects to a company VPN: Authentication confirms their identity via credentials. Authorization determines which internal systems they can reach. Accounting logs exactly which servers they accessed, when, and for how long.</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Real Life — Internet Service Provider:</strong> When you dial up or connect via ISP: Authentication verifies your account. Authorization grants internet bandwidth according to your plan. Accounting tracks your data usage for billing.</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Real Life — University Network:</strong> Students login to campus WiFi (Authentication), can only access learning resources matching their course enrollment (Authorization), and their bandwidth usage is tracked and limited per policy (Accounting).</div>

          <div class="section-label">Step-by-Step Process</div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-text">Authentication: Verify the user's identity</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-text">Authorization: Grant appropriate permissions</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-text">Accounting: Log all actions and resource usage</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-text">Reports generated for audit and billing</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-text">Anomalies trigger security alerts</div></div>

