      <!-- ── 5. 2FA ───────────────────────────────── -->
      <section class="topic-section" id="twofa">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <i class="ti ti-device-mobile" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:20px"></i>
            2FA
            <span class="badge badge-amber">Security</span>
          </div>
          <p class="definition">Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) is a specific subset of MFA that uses exactly two verification factors. It's the most widely deployed form of multi-factor authentication and is now standard across major consumer platforms. The most common combination is password + SMS/app code.</p>

          <div class="section-label">How it works — Flow Diagram</div>
          <svg class="flow-svg" viewBox="0 0 640 150" role="img">
