      <!-- ── 6. OTP ───────────────────────────────── -->
      <section class="topic-section" id="otp">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <i class="ti ti-number" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:20px"></i>
            OTP
            <span class="badge badge-green">Mechanism</span>
          </div>
          <p class="definition">A One-Time Password (OTP) is a password valid for only one login session or transaction. It cannot be reused, which means intercepted or stolen OTPs are useless. They're generated either by a time-based algorithm (TOTP) or an event counter (HOTP) and are central to MFA/2FA implementations.</p>

          <div class="section-label">How it works — Flow Diagram</div>
          <svg class="flow-svg" viewBox="0 0 640 170" role="img">
            <title>TOTP OTP Generation</title>
            <defs>
