      <!-- ── 8. ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL (RBAC) ── -->
      <section class="topic-section" id="rbac">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <i class="ti ti-users" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:20px"></i>
            Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
            <span class="badge badge-green">Framework</span>
          </div>
          <p class="definition">Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) is an authorization mechanism where permissions are assigned to specific roles (e.g., Administrator, Editor, Viewer) rather than directly to individual users. Users are then assigned roles, inheriting their permissions. This makes access management scalable and structured.</p>

