      <!-- ── 9. SINGLE SIGN-ON (SSO) ─────────────── -->
      <section class="topic-section" id="sso">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <i class="ti ti-login" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:20px"></i>
            Single Sign-On (SSO)
            <span class="badge badge-green">Framework</span>
          </div>
          <p class="definition">Single Sign-On (SSO) is an authentication method that enables users to authenticate once and securely access multiple independent applications or websites. It relies on a central Identity Provider (IdP) that passes assertions/tokens to Service Providers (SP) via protocols like SAML or OpenID Connect (OIDC).</p>

          <div class="section-label">How it works — Flow Diagram</div>
          <svg class="flow-svg" viewBox="0 0 640 180" role="img">
            <title>SSO Flow</title>
