            <span class="tag">SAML 2.0</span>
            <span class="tag">OpenID Connect (OIDC)</span>
            <span class="tag">Federated Identity</span>
            <span class="tag">OAuth 2.0</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── 10. PRIVILEGED ACCESS MANAGEMENT (PAM) ── -->
      <section class="topic-section" id="pam">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <i class="ti ti-user-shield" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:20px"></i>
            Privileged Access Management (PAM)
            <span class="badge badge-green">Framework</span>
          </div>
          <p class="definition">Privileged Access Management (PAM) is a system of policies, processes, and tools designed to secure, monitor, and audit administrative accounts (e.g. root, domain admin) that have high-level privileges. PAM ensures these keys to the kingdom are strictly controlled and session-recorded.</p>

          <div class="section-label">How it works — Flow Diagram</div>
          <svg class="flow-svg" viewBox="0 0 640 180" role="img">
            <title>PAM Flow</title>
            <defs>
              <marker id="arr10" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
