              <text class="ts" x="80" y="105" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Needs Root Access</text>
            </g>
            <line x1="140" y1="90" x2="195" y2="90" class="arr" stroke="#8b96a5" marker-end="url(#arr10)"></line>
            <text class="ts" x="167" y="82" text-anchor="middle">1. Request</text>

            <g class="c-purple">
              <rect x="195" y="55" width="160" height="70" rx="8" stroke-width="0.5"></rect>
              <text class="th" x="275" y="75" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">PAM Gateway</text>
              <text class="ts" x="275" y="95" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Rotates &amp; Obscures</text>
              <text class="ts" x="275" y="111" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Creds (JIT Access)</text>
            </g>
            
            <line x1="355" y1="90" x2="410" y2="90" class="arr" stroke="#8b96a5" marker-end="url(#arr10)"></line>
            <text class="ts" x="382" y="82" text-anchor="middle">2. Proxies</text>
            
            <g class="c-teal">
              <rect x="410" y="65" width="120" height="50" rx="8" stroke-width="0.5"></rect>
              <text class="th" x="470" y="87" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Target Server</text>
              <text class="ts" x="470" y="105" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Production DB</text>
            </g>
            
            <line x1="275" y1="125" x2="275" y2="155" class="arr" stroke="#cf222e" marker-end="url(#arr10)"></line>
            <line x1="275" y1="155" x2="540" y2="155" class="arr" stroke="#cf222e" marker-end="url(#arr10)"></line>
            
            <g class="c-red">
              <rect x="540" y="65" width="90" height="90" rx="8" stroke-width="0.5"></rect>
              <text class="th" x="585" y="100" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Audit Logs</text>
              <text class="ts" x="585" y="120" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Keystroke &amp;</text>
              <text class="ts" x="585" y="136" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Video Record</text>
            </g>
            <line x1="530" y1="90" x2="540" y2="90" class="arr" stroke="#1a7f37" marker-end="url(#arr10)"></line>
          </svg>

          <div class="section-label">Real-Life Examples</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Real Life — Password Vaulting:</strong> Administrators do not know the actual root passwords of production servers. The passwords are saved in a PAM vault (like CyberArk) and rotated automatically every 24 hours. The PAM proxy injects the credentials transparently at login.</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Real Life — Just-In-Time (JIT) Access:</strong> A database engineer needs access to billing tables for an hour. They request access through a PAM workflow. Once approved, PAM elevates their permissions and automatically revokes them after 60 minutes.</div>
          <div class="example-box"><strong>Everyday App — SSH Session Recording:</strong> Security teams use PAM tools to record visual SSH/RDP sessions of contractors working on critical infrastructure, allowing them to playback keystrokes to detect suspicious acts.</div>

          <div class="section-label">Step-by-Step Process</div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-text">Admin requests elevated credentials from the PAM system</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-text">PAM validates request against policy or prompts manager for approval</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-text">Access granted via dynamic, short-lived session (Just-In-Time)</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-text">PAM records all activities (keystrokes, commands, screens)</div></div>
          <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-text">Session closes, and PAM rolls/rotates the target account credentials</div></div>

          <div class="section-label">Strengths &amp; Weaknesses</div>
          <div class="pros-cons">
            <div class="pros">
              <div class="pros-title">Strengths</div>
              <div class="pc-item">+ Minimizes target surface for credentials theft</div>
              <div class="pc-item">+ Implements bulletproof session auditing and attribution</div>
              <div class="pc-item">+ Stops lateral movement by compromised accounts</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cons">
              <div class="cons-title">Limitations</div>
              <div class="pc-item">− High implementation costs and organizational friction</div>
              <div class="pc-item">− Admin bypass routes can compromise security if not hardened</div>
              <div class="pc-item">− High operational complexity to customize workflows</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="section-label">Related Terms</div>
