            <span class="tag">Credential Rotation</span>
            <span class="tag">JIT (Just-In-Time) Access</span>
            <span class="tag">Bastion Host</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── 11. PRINCIPLE OF LEAST PRIVILEGE ────── -->
      <section class="topic-section" id="leastprivilege">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <i class="ti ti-scale" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:20px"></i>
            Principle of Least Privilege (PoLP)
            <span class="badge badge-green">Framework</span>
          </div>
          <p class="definition">The Principle of Least Privilege (PoLP) dictates that a user, program, or system should be granted only the minimum necessary privileges required to complete its tasks. By limiting permissions to what is essential, you minimize the risk and "blast radius" of user errors or account hijacking.</p>

          <div class="section-label">How it works — Over-Privileged vs. Least Privilege</div>
          <svg class="flow-svg" viewBox="0 0 640 180" role="img">
